       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg per day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day for inpatients under physician supervision. For OTC use the maximum is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg QID, please confirm that and give a brief rationale for the note. I'd still want to be sure it's intentional before entering it."
